  "description": "T1.  London plane: Reduce the lateral crown by up to 4m on the N (for the longest branches) and about 2m on the NE, with about 2m reduction elsewhere to balance the crown so far as feasible while reducing the new impact of wind on the tree, tapering into the upper crown.  No overall height reduction to be carried out. T2.  London plane: Fell and grind out the roots to about 300mm below existing ground level. T3. London plane: Selectively reduce and lift branches oversailing the highway, especially ESE, to their last reduction points over the road to provide about 4m vertical clearance underneath. T35.  Malus: Fell and grind out the roots to about 300mm below existing ground level.\r",
